{"term":{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SO_0001484","compactId":"SO_0001484","id":"SO:0001484","label":"X_element_combinatorial_repeat","definition":{"text":"An X element combinatorial repeat is a repeat region located between the X element and the telomere or adjacent Y' element.","xrefs":["http://www.yeastgenome.org/help/glossary.html"]},"comments":["X element combinatorial repeats contain Tbf1p binding sites, and possible functions include a role in telomerase-independent telomere maintenance via recombination or as a barrier against transcriptional silencing. These are usually present as a combination of one or more of several types of smaller elements (designated A, B, C, or D). This term was requested 2009-10-16 by Michel Dumontier, tracker id 2880747."],"synonyms":[{"scope":"exact","value":"INSDC_qualifier:x_element_combinatorial_repeat"},{"scope":"exact","value":"X element combinatorial repeat"},{"scope":"broad","value":"INSDC_feature:repeat_region"}],"xrefs":[],"subsets":[],"altIds":[],"namespace":"sequence","isObsolete":false,"replacedBy":[],"canonicalUrl":"/browser/current_release/term/SO:0001484/","history":{"firstSeen":{"hash":"92e3cae9f3d39e5979110bad332c5fadf7a4b3ab","shortHash":"92e3cae","date":"2016-12-05","subject":"Add renamed SO files","issueRefs":[]},"mostRecent":{"hash":"5fe48bd4b720f8b140cb0f77461798c55532c097","shortHash":"5fe48bd","date":"2018-01-26","subject":"Add INSDC mappings","issueRefs":[]},"entries":[{"hash":"5fe48bd4b720f8b140cb0f77461798c55532c097","shortHash":"5fe48bd","date":"2018-01-26","subject":"Add INSDC mappings","issueRefs":[]},{"hash":"92e3cae9f3d39e5979110bad332c5fadf7a4b3ab","shortHash":"92e3cae","date":"2016-12-05","subject":"Add renamed SO files","issueRefs":[]}],"semanticEvents":[{"type":"synonym_added","date":"2018-01-26","commit":"5fe48bd4b720f8b140cb0f77461798c55532c097","shortHash":"5fe48bd","subject":"Add INSDC mappings","summary":"Synonym added: INSDC_qualifier:x_element_combinatorial_repeat","details":["S